  "id": "DrugBank_DB00637 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Astemizole is linked to Allergic Rhinitis through a chain of indications that involve Vasomotor Rhinitis. This pathway suggests that Astemizole may exert its effects on the nasal mucosa, potentially modulating inflammatory responses associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of Vasomotor Rhinitis in all three paths, which in turn is linked to Allergic Rhinitis. The mechanisms appear to involve the modulation of vascular tone and inflammatory mediators, possibly through the action of Astemizole on histamine receptors or other pathways. The presence of multiple distinct agents—such as Mizolastine and Ramatroban—suggests that Astemizole may act as a general modulator of vasomotor symptoms, with different agents targeting different aspects of the inflammatory response. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Astemizole to be repurposed for the treatment of allergic rhinitis, based on its ability to influence the underlying pathophysiology of the condition.",
